@inject ApiMetadata Api
@* SplitButton's Overview, written by hand after Button's: the main action and its menu, links and
   downloads, icon only, its looks and states, OnClick, a Toolbar, and what it does without script.
   Accessibility and See also come from the doc comment. *@

<Heading Level="2">Usage</Heading>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Usage</Code>
<TextBlock>A SplitButton has a main action and, beside it, an arrow that opens a menu of related ones. Clicking the main button only runs its action, and the arrow only opens the menu. Use it when one action is the usual one; when none is, use a <Anchor Href="docs/components/menu">Menu</Anchor>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">The main action and its menu</Heading>
<TextBlock>The main button acts like a <Anchor Href="docs/components/button">Button</Anchor>: to post a form, set <Code>Submit</Code>, <Code>Name</Code> and <Code>Value</Code>. For the other choices, put <Code>MenuItem</Code>s inside the SplitButton. To name the arrow for screen readers, set <Code>MenuLabel</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="split-button-actions" />
<TextBlock>Choosing an item runs that item, and the main action stays as it was. The SplitButton doesn't remember the last choice. To make it the default, change <Code>Label</Code> and <Code>Href</Code> or <Code>OnClick</Code> yourself.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Links and downloads</Heading>
<TextBlock>To make the main button a link, set <Code>Href</Code>. To open the link in a new tab, set <Code>External</Code> too. Other attributes, such as <Code>download</Code>, go to the main button.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="split-button-links" />

<Heading Level="2">Only an icon</Heading>
<TextBlock>To show only the main button's icon, set <Code>IconOnly</Code> with a <Code>StartIcon</Code>. The <Code>Label</Code> stays as the button's name and tooltip.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="split-button-icon-only" />

<Heading Level="2">Colors, weights and sizes</Heading>
<TextBlock>To style both parts together, set <Code>Accent</Code>, <Code>Variant</Code> and <Code>Size</Code>. To make the main button fill the container, set <Code>FullWidth</Code>. Any of these you leave unset come from a <Anchor Href="docs/components/button-group">ButtonGroup</Anchor> or <Anchor Href="docs/components/toolbar">Toolbar</Anchor> around it.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="split-button-looks" />

<Heading Level="2">In a row of buttons</Heading>
<TextBlock>To join a SplitButton to other buttons, put it in a <Anchor Href="docs/components/button-group">ButtonGroup</Anchor>. Only the row's outer ends are rounded, and the SplitButton gets the group's look.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="split-button-in-group" />

<Heading Level="2">States</Heading>
<TextBlock>When there's no usual action but the others still work, set <Code>MainDisabled</Code>. When there's nothing else to choose, set <Code>MenuDisabled</Code>. To disable the whole control, or show it loading, set <Code>Disabled</Code> or <Code>Loading</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="split-button-states" />

<Heading Level="2">Where the menu opens</Heading>
<TextBlock>By default, the menu lines up with the start edge of the whole button. To open it elsewhere, set <Code>Placement</Code>. For long items, set <Code>PanelWidth</Code>, as on a Menu.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="split-button-panel-width" />

<Heading Level="2">Running C# on click</Heading>
<TextBlock>On interactive pages, the main button and each <Code>MenuItem</Code> can run C# when clicked. Set <Code>OnClick</Code> on each.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="split-button-on-click" />

<Heading Level="2">In a Toolbar</Heading>
<TextBlock>In a <Anchor Href="docs/components/toolbar">Toolbar</Anchor>, use <Code>ToolbarSplitButton</Code>. It accepts a toolbar item's <Code>Position</Code>, <Code>Priority</Code> and <Code>Overflow</Code>. In the … menu, it becomes a submenu named by <Code>MenuLabel</Code>, with the main action as its first item, then the same items.</TextBlock>
<TextBlock>With the toolbar's <Code>CollapseLabels</Code>, the main button drops its text and keeps its icon. <Anchor Href="docs/components/toolbar/actions#ex-toolbar-split-button">See it on the Toolbar's page</Anchor>, and narrow the window to see the items move.</TextBlock>
<Code Block Language="razor">@InToolbar</Code>

<Heading Level="2">With JavaScript off</Heading>
<TextBlock>With <Anchor Href="docs/common/render-modes">JavaScript off</Anchor>, the arrow still opens and closes the menu, and links and form posts work on the main button and on the items, as on a Menu. Alt+Down and the arrow keys require IzzyBlazor's script; without it, Tab to the arrow and press Enter. <Code>OnClick</Code> runs only on interactive pages.</TextBlock>

@if (OverviewParts.Of(Component, Api).Count > 0)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Parts</Heading>
}
<OverviewParts Component="Component" />

<Heading Level="2">Mode support</Heading>
<ModeSupportTable Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@if (ApiComponent.Accessibility is not null)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Accessibility</Heading>
    <DocHtml Html="@ApiComponent.Accessibility" Context="@(Context with { Overview = true })" Size="ProseSize.Md" />
}

@KeyboardTable.Section(ApiComponent)

<Heading Level="2">Parameters</Heading>
<ParameterTable ApiComponent="ApiComponent" ApiHref="@Registry.ApiPageHref(Component)" Context="Context" Compact />

<OverviewSeeAlso Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RegistryComponent Component { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiComponent ApiComponent { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiPageContext Context { get; set; } = null!;

    private const string Usage = """
        <SplitButton Label="Save" StartIcon="Lucide.Save" OnClick="Save" MenuLabel="More save options">
            <MenuItem OnClick="SaveAs">Save as…</MenuItem>
            <MenuItem Href="/drafts">Open drafts</MenuItem>
        </SplitButton>

        @* A link and a download, which work with no script *@
        <SplitButton Label="Download PDF" Href="/report.pdf" download MenuLabel="Other formats">
            <MenuItem Href="/report.csv" download>CSV</MenuItem>
        </SplitButton>
        """;

    private const string InToolbar = """
        <Toolbar Label="Document">
            <ToolbarSplitButton Label="Save" StartIcon="Lucide.Save" Submit MenuLabel="More save options" Priority="1">
                <MenuItem Submit Name="intent" Value="draft">Save as draft</MenuItem>
            </ToolbarSplitButton>
        </Toolbar>
        """;
}
